Owner ruling on WI-hupod. A module-less external stub and its typed twin
are the same call seen by two producers; §11 made them two edges on
3,973 of 4,133 method-call sites under scip-python.

§15 refines §11 rather than excepting it. For an endpoint outside the
repo the identity is dst_ref — ADR-0037 ruling 2 already says so — which
can abstain, and not the dst string, whose module segment defaults to
the "external" sentinel that ADR-0051's MODULE_KEY_AXIOM defines as not
a marker for the absence of an answer. An external identity key missing
its module component is partial; a partial key matches a complete one
that agrees on every component it states, and two partial keys do not
match each other.

Placement is before deduplicate_edges and before create_boundary_nodes,
both load-bearing: 12,126 external call edges are post-collapse
multi-site (4,818 sentinel-module), and 779 of 2,137 external_symbol
nodes carry a sentinel module absorbing 22,284 of 74,816 in-edges.
Ambiguity is refused, not guessed — 10 of 86,839 site groups here.

§11 additionally loses a sentence that scip-python falsified ("SCIP
emits no external edges today") and gains the in-repo qualification.

Ruled, not implemented: WI-hupod, blocked by INV-difud.

